      "writtenOn": "2021-09-10T22:24:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Are you referencing, \"Tell Device Policy Manager to perform Data Reset\" from the state diagram? That hadn\u0027t caught my eye, and I don\u0027t immediately see anywhere else where it says the DFP does this.\n\nAs a threshold issue, it seems entirely superfluous to do this in the DPM with its current design, in lockstep with the PE. With an independent DPM, this state would get more complicated by outsourcing the Data Reset, and I\u0027m not sure what that would get us in terms of separation of concerns.\n\nIf the spec didn\u0027t say which component did this, which one would you want to do it? If the PE sounds like as good a place as any, what if we left it this way, and I deleted \"Tell Device Policy Manager to\" in my ECR?",
      "parentUuid": "632bfbc8_96cae6e0",
      "revId": "27afb0a54303da5a475550816f09bb7750b89add",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
