      "writtenOn": "2021-09-10T22:24:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I wasn\u0027t, but I am a bit now.\n\nI think the most reasonable interpretation of the process in 6.3.14 is that it describes the entire Data Reset process, not the behavior in a particular state. (As a side note, I think this list of steps should go in the description of the *process* in 6.8.2, not the description of the message.) Step 3) Reset the cable would potentially start in PE_DDR_Wait_for_VCONN_Off and finish in PE_DDR_Perform_Data_Reset.\n\nBut that would imply that steps 1) and 2) take place in PE_DDR_Send_Data_Reset, presumably after receiving the Accept. (They could also happen at the very beginning of Wait_for_VCONN_Off or Perform_Data_Reset, depending on the initial VCONN Source, but that sounds pointlessly complicated.)\n\nThat implication is not reflected in the state diagram, and if it\u0027s correct, \"Tell the Device Policy Manager to perform Data Reset\" from the diagram would be ambiguous.\n\nIt\u0027s probably worth checking with the WG.",
      "parentUuid": "ce073a76_a5d464a0",
      "revId": "27afb0a54303da5a475550816f09bb7750b89add",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
