      "lineNbr": 7167,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-10T22:24:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As discussed elsewhere, I suspect that the intent of the spec was not that it be checked in all states.\n\nIf we used a parent state, and the intent were as I suspect, then the children of the parent state would be PE_DDR_Wait_for_VCONN_Off and PE_DDR_Perform_Data_Reset. This design would cause the timer to start at the beginning of either of those states as opposed to the end of PE_DDR_Send_Data_Reset, as specified. The timer is long enough that that probably wouldn\u0027t really matter.\n\nI\u0027d lean towards not using a parent state to conform more closely to the spec. If we wanted the spec to support an easier implementation (for us), I could submit an ECR that says to start it at the beginning of those two states instead of the end of Send_Data_Reset.",
      "parentUuid": "fe444473_cf0e1e14",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 7167,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 7167,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "27afb0a54303da5a475550816f09bb7750b89add",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "24e4c754_87fec3c4",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 7167,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-16T21:24:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was thinking the parent state\u0027s only job would be to check for expiration and run error recovery, not start the timer.  Just to reduce code duplication if the timer expiration needs checked in multiple states.  But it\u0027s up to you.",
      "parentUuid": "a2e22ecc_a2953a69",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 7167,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 7167,
        "endChar": 55
