        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-01T04:32:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I vote error recovery on discard.  That seems like a protocol error if the partner sent a new message in the middle of this",
      "revId": "27afb0a54303da5a475550816f09bb7750b89add",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "43660f64_6229c4ec",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 7179,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-10T22:24:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think you\u0027re probably right. Note, however, that Godzilla Creek, the only USB4 implementation I have access to, responds Not Supported to Data Reset Complete. I haven\u0027t seen it interrupt the process, but I\u0027m not sure what to expect.\n\nIt also feels a bit draconian to go into Error Recovery after they interrupted a process that, from both of our points of view, was already done.\n\n(As a side note, I was originally just firing and forgetting this from the exit function, because that\u0027s what the spec suggests that we do. I only added this check because our code was sending a PRS and discarding this. Since Godzilla Creek is clearly not waiting for it, I don\u0027t have any evidence of what could be expected to happen if we don\u0027t send it. The spec implies that the UFP is supposed to wait forever. I\u0027m feeling another ECR coming.)",
      "parentUuid": "dedfef4c_5eefc1b6",
      "revId": "27afb0a54303da5a475550816f09bb7750b89add",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "13bd72c4_64a9a111",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 7179,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-16T21:24:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is Godzilla Creek sending a message before we can send Data_Reset_Complete?  I\u0027d only expect discard if we tried sending Data_Reset_Complete and a message came in before we could do this.\n\nWell, if you want to get involved in some PD WG ECRs, I wouldn\u0027t object :)",
      "parentUuid": "43660f64_6229c4ec",
      "revId": "27afb0a54303da5a475550816f09bb7750b89add",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
